# /etc/inet/network-config -- sourced by /etc/init.d/inetinit after the
# interfaces are started.
#
# The interfaces themselves are set up from /etc/inet/interfaces by ifup; see
# interfaces(4). This file is kept, empty, for instructions written for the
# stock system that say "add this line to network-config". Lines added here
# run at every boot, as root, after "ifup -a" has been started in the
# background, so an interface may not be up yet when they run.
